    pr_ref:  # e2b8
    description: ""  # e2b8
    fields:  # e2b8
      statement: "Most linkers emit a single hardcoded confidence value across all their edges: decorator-dispatch always 0.7 (292 edges, 1 value), dependency-linker always 0.9 (26 edges, 1 value), enclosure-linker always 0.9 (119 edges, 1 value), pyffi-linker always 0.75, database-query-linker always 0.85, json always 0.95. Only type-hierarchy uses real variance (12 unique values across 324 edges). The confidence field exists, is 100% populated, but doesn't reflect per-edge uncertainty — it's just a per-linker label."  # e2b8
      root_cause: "Linkers were ported with hardcoded confidence constants. No calibration step computes per-edge confidence based on resolution method, ambiguity, or evidence quality."  # e2b8
